## 4.1 MLflow Default Credentials

### F-01   models.smarthire.htb -- default credentials admin:password - CRITICAL

| Field | Detail |
|-------|--------|
| Description | MLflow 2.14.1 was deployed on `models.smarthire.htb` with HTTP Basic Auth using the documented default credentials `admin:password`. These were never changed after enabling authentication. Any party who discovers the subdomain has full read and write access to the experiment tracking server and all model artifact stores. |
| Prerequisites | Network access to `models.smarthire.htb`. No prior credentials required beyond the public default. |
| Impact | Full read and write access to the MLflow artifact store for all tracked runs. Enables artifact replacement attacks and model poisoning across any hosted model. |
| Affected system | smarthire.htb -- `models.smarthire.htb` MLflow 2.14.1 |
| CVSS 3.1 | 9.8 -- AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H |
| CWE | CWE-1392: Use of Default Credentials |

**Steps to reproduce:**

1. `curl -sk -u admin:password http://models.smarthire.htb/`
2. Observe full access to the MLflow API and artifact store.

**Evidence:**

```
$ curl -sk -u admin:password http://models.smarthire.htb/api/2.0/mlflow/experiments/list
{"experiments":[{"experiment_id":"0","name":"Default",...}]}
```

**Remediation:** Change the MLflow HTTP Basic Auth password to a randomly generated strong credential immediately. Restrict access to the models subdomain to authorised internal IP ranges at the network layer. Rotate any API tokens or credentials that were accessible from the artifact store.

**Verification:** Confirm the default credentials no longer grant access. Confirm the subdomain is not reachable from untrusted networks. Verify the changed password meets the organisation's complexity requirements.

